  "text": "The extract under this heading is the closing of the fairy queen article. The queen Clídna counseled the local ruler Cormac MacCarthy on a lawsuit. At daybreak he kissed a stone as she instructed. He gained instant eloquence and spoke his way free of the case. To keep others from the same advantage, MacCarthy set the stone high in an unnumbered reach of the castle wall. It rests there still. Sightseers now hang upside down to kiss the stone and claim Clídna's gift.",
